// Behavioral API documentation for the §2254 habeas workspace canister.
//
// Static Markdown authored from the current backend source. AI assistants read
// it through the ICP MCP connector alongside the Candid interface to call the
// app's methods on the user's behalf.

mixin () {
  public query func getApiDoc() : async Text {
    "## Purpose\n\n"
    # "A per-user pro se federal habeas corpus workspace under 28 U.S.C. § 2254 for U.S. litigants. "
    # "Each signed-in user keeps their own projects, uploaded case files, indexed passages, legal drafts, "
    # "citation checks and model provider key. Nothing is shared between users.\n\n"
    # "## Authentication and identity\n\n"
    # "- Every workspace method requires a signed (non-anonymous) caller. Anonymous callers are rejected.\n"
    # "- This is a single-owner workspace: the first principal to complete Internet Identity sign-in becomes the owner (`#admin`). "
    # "Every workspace endpoint is owner-only; any other principal is rejected with the trap "
    # "\"This workspace belongs to its owner. Remix your own copy from the Caffeine App Market.\"\n"
    # "- Registration prerequisite: a direct API caller must first call `_initialize_access_control` once as a signed-in caller "
    # "(or complete `_internet_identity_sign_in_start` / `_internet_identity_sign_in_finish`). The first initializer receives `#admin`; "
    # "later callers receive `#user` and are then refused by the owner gate. An unregistered caller is refused with the same owner trap; "
    # "an anonymous caller is refused with \"Unauthorized: sign in to use this workspace\".\n"
    # "- The frontend pins an Internet Identity derivation origin, published at `/.well-known/ii-derivation-origin`. "
    # "An agent holding the user's Internet Identity authorization derives the correct per-app principal against that origin "
    # "(for example `icp identity link web <name> --app <host>`). Such a delegation acts with the user's full authority in this app until it expires.\n\n"
    # "## Units and encodings\n\n"
    # "- Timestamps are signed `Int` nanoseconds since the Unix epoch (`Time.now()`).\n"
    # "- Ids, page numbers, paragraph numbers and counters are `Nat`.\n"
    # "- `blob` fields are object-storage references (`Blob`).\n"
    # "- `?T` fields are optional; `null` means absent.\n"
    # "- Variants: `IndexingStatus` is `#pending | #indexing | #indexed | #failed({reason})`; "
    # "`RetrievalResult` is `#found({passages}) | #notFoundInLibrary`; "
    # "`GroundedAnswer` is `#answered({answer, passages}) | #notFoundInLibrary`; "
    # "`KeyValidation` is `#valid | #invalid({reason})`.\n\n"
    # "## Projects\n\n"
    # "- `createProject(input)` / `renameProject(id, input)` — `input` is `{name, caption}`; name 1–120 chars, caption ≤ 400 chars.\n"
    # "- `listProjects()` — newest activity first; `fileCount` and `indexingStatus` are derived from the project's files.\n"
    # "- `deleteProject(id)` — deletes the project and every case file and passage inside it. Destructive and not reversible.\n\n"
    # "## Case files and indexing\n\n"
    # "- `registerCaseFile(input)` — registers an upload and indexes it. `input` carries `projectId, filename, mimeType, sizeBytes, pageCount, blob, extractedText`. "
    # "The browser extracts the text; a file with no extracted text is marked `#failed` with a reason. "
    # "Re-uploading a filename already in the project creates a new version and drops the old passages.\n"
    # "- `listCaseFiles(projectId)` — newest upload first.\n"
    # "- `getFilePassages(fileId, start)` — one page of 50 passages in document order, plus `total`.\n"
    # "- `deleteCaseFile(fileId)` — deletes the file and its passages. Destructive.\n"
    # "- `retryFileIndexing(fileId)` — re-runs indexing for a `#failed` file only; traps otherwise.\n"
    # "- Indexing is synchronous within `registerCaseFile` / `retryFileIndexing`: the returned file already carries its final status. "
    # "Poll `listCaseFiles` or `listProjects` to observe status.\n\n"
    # "## Retrieval and grounded answers\n\n"
    # "- `retrievePassages(request)` — `request` is `{scope, question}` where `scope` is `#project(id)` or `#library`. "
    # "Returns the best supporting passages with file, page and paragraph locators, or `#notFoundInLibrary` when the library holds nothing supporting the question.\n"
    # "- `answerFromLibrary(request)` — same scope; when supporting passages exist, the caller's own model key is used to write an answer strictly from those passages, "
    # "returned with the cited passages. Returns `#notFoundInLibrary` when nothing supports the question. "
    # "Traps with \"Save your model provider key before asking a grounded question\" when no key is saved. "
    # "This is an update call that performs an external model request; it is not idempotent and may be slow.\n\n"
    # "## Drafts\n\n"
    # "- `createDraft(input)` — `input` is `{projectId, draftType, title}`; `draftType` is `#petition | #memorandum | #motion | #reply | #noticeOfExhaustion`. "
    # "A new draft opens with the default outline for its type.\n"
    # "- `getDraft(id)`, `listDrafts(projectId)` (newest autosave first).\n"
    # "- `autosaveDraft(id, content)` — `content` is `{title, sections}`; snapshots the previous state into version history (bounded to 20 versions).\n"
    # "- `restoreDraftVersion(id, version)` — restores a saved version, snapshotting the current state first.\n"
    # "- `deleteDraft(id)` — destructive.\n\n"
    # "## Citations and grounding\n\n"
    # "- `checkDraftCitations(draftId)` — finds reporter citations (e.g. \"550 U.S. 465\", \"28 U.S.C. § 2254\") and marks each `#verifiedInLibrary(citedPassage)` or `#unverified`.\n"
    # "- `checkDraftGrounding(draftId)` — lists sentences that make a claim but cite no library passage.\n"
    # "- Citation results are advisory research assistance, not legal advice.\n\n"
    # "## DOCX export\n\n"
    # "- `exportDraftDocx(draftId, options)` — `options` is `{caption, disclaimer}`. Returns `{filename, bytes}` where `bytes` is a DOCX (ZIP) document "
    # "with the caption block, numbered sections, a source appendix of verified citations and the disclaimer.\n\n"
    # "## Model key (BYOK)\n\n"
    # "- `saveModelKey(key)` — validates the pasted provider key's shape and stores it. The full key is never returned; only its last four characters are ever reported.\n"
    # "- `getModelKeyStatus()` — `{configured, last4}`.\n"
    # "- `removeModelKey()` — removes the saved key.\n\n"
    # "## Attestation\n\n"
    # "- `getAttestation()` — `{confirmed, confirmedAt}`.\n"
    # "- `confirmAttestation()` — records that the user confirmed they are in the United States and proceeding pro se.\n\n"
    # "## Conversation history (chat surface)\n\n"
    # "- `listConversations()`, `getConversationPage(id, start)` (25 messages per page, oldest first), "
    # "`recordExchange(conversationId, userContent, assistantContent)` (null id starts a new conversation), "
    # "`setConversationSummary(id, coversCount, content)`, `deleteConversation(id)`.\n"
    # "- `getInferenceCredentials()` mints a short-lived ephemeral inference key for the caller; `isInferenceConfigured()` reports whether the platform provisioned credentials.\n\n"
    # "## OQL data access (schema / execute)\n\n"
    # "- `schema()` returns a JSON document describing the queryable tables; `execute(qJson)` runs a JSON query and returns typed rows.\n"
    # "- Tables: `project`, `caseFile`, `passage`, `draft`. Each row carries an `owner` principal column plus the stored record's fields "
    # "(for `draft`, `draftType` is the tag text and `sectionCount` the number of sections; file bytes and extracted text are not exposed).\n"
    # "- Authorization is per table and scoped to the caller: a signed-in caller reads only its own rows, the platform controller reads all, "
    # "and an anonymous caller is denied. A caller never sees another user's rows, directly or through a join.\n\n"
    # "## Mutation retry safety and gotchas\n\n"
    # "- `registerCaseFile` is not idempotent: calling it twice with the same filename creates a new version each time.\n"
    # "- `autosaveDraft` appends a version snapshot on every call; repeated identical calls still consume version history.\n"
    # "- Delete operations are destructive and cannot be undone.\n"
    # "- `answerFromLibrary` and `getInferenceCredentials` perform external HTTP calls and are not idempotent; do not auto-retry them.\n"
    # "- `execute` is a query: it never mutates state, so it is safe to retry.\n"
    # "- Errors surface as traps (rejects) with a readable message; the caller cannot branch on them programmatically.\n";
  };
};
